# What the A2 polish wave changed, through the real keys and from a normal
# start: the Burning's vents, the crowns of the scrapwood, the machines' cuts in
# the turf, a machine with mass at the distance a player sees it, a wrap made in
# the HAND with no bench against a cold that now comes on with the dusk the sky
# draws, and the targeting tag over a body in the world.
#
#   tools/tour.sh tours/polish.tour --seed=7 --hour=11 --weather=clear:0 \
#     --give=rag:5,wrack:4,pitch:1
#
# Every frame here says what it is OF, because a frame of a vent that holds no
# vent is worse evidence than no frame at all.
coast calm

# --- The Burning's vents ------------------------------------------------------
# A solid pure-white disc ~14x10 native pixels, nine identical ones to a frame
# and the only pure white in the landscape. Now: a broken clinker collar, plates
# of crust floating on the fire with amber between them, and a core a third the
# width. At noon, and then at night, where each one lays its own pool.
place burning
wait 1.2
shot 01-the-burning-at-noon with land:burning
at prop:vent
zoom 5
wait 1.0
shot 02-a-hole-in-the-ground with prop:vent
hour 23
weather clear:0
wait 1.4
shot 03-a-vent-at-night with prop:vent
zoom 12
wait 0.8
shot 04-the-vents-in-the-dark with land:burning

# --- The scrapwood's crowns ---------------------------------------------------
# Thirty near-identical mushrooms at one scale, each with the same ruled bar
# across it. Six trees now, each with its own height, spread, arms and bar.
coast calm
hour 11
weather clear:0
place scrapwood
wait 1.4
shot 05-a-wood-and-not-a-texture with land:scrapwood
near scrap_tree
zoom 6
wait 1.0
shot 06-one-tree-of-six with prop:scrap_tree
zoom 12

# --- The machines' cuts in the turf -------------------------------------------
# Four or five bars of identical width at identical spacing with the same grain
# in each. The order is still ruled; the ladder is not stamped any more.
# Borders this seed holds since a landscape stands whole on one continent (GEN 24).
place coast-moss
wait 1.4
shot 07-the-cuts-are-work-not-a-stamp with border:coast-moss

# --- A machine with mass at the distance a player sees it ---------------------
# The watcher: close up the best-drawn thing in the roster, from a hill away a
# thin mast and three splayed legs of scattered pixels. A wide drum with a rivet
# row, a housing with a slit on the cross bar, and a shade over the head.
place coast
wait 1.2
spawn watcher
wait 1.2
shot 08-a-watcher-at-play-distance with mob:watcher
# ...and the tag it carries, which is made of the slate's glass now and not of
# an opaque black lozenge.
hold target
await target 5
wait 0.9
shot 09-read-through-the-slate with mob:watcher
release target
wait 1.2
coast calm
wait 0.8

# --- Day two, with a knife and no bench ---------------------------------------
# A warm wrap was a BENCH recipe, a day's walk and a day's building behind the
# snowfield it answers. It is hand work, like the rest of the made tier.
try 3
tap craft
await app:crafting 3
end
wait 0.4
shot 10-the-made-tier-in-the-hand with app:crafting
choose wrap_warm
tap use
await made 8
wait 0.5
# ...and the wadding that goes in its socket, out of rags and dried wrack. The
# snowfield in a wind wants both, and both are hand work.
choose mod_wadding
tap use
await made 8
wait 0.5
shot 11-a-wrap-and-its-wadding-made-by-hand with app:crafting
tap pause
await app:none 4

# --- And the cold that comes on with the dusk the sky draws --------------------
# FightRules.nightfall was flat zero until 20:00 while dusk was drawn from
# 18:30, so a body stood in a visibly deep dusk carrying noon's cold. One curve
# now, and eight in the evening is where the two used to disagree most: the old
# line was still flat at 0.43 there, which is felt and no more, and this one has
# the snowfield past HARM on a body with nothing on it.
place snowfield
hour 20
weather clear:0
wait 2.0
await cold 20
await pressure_bites 40
shot 12-a-snowfield-at-eight-in-the-evening with pressure_bites,land:snowfield
# The wrap goes on where the player is standing, and the cold comes off.
tap pause
wait 0.8
choose loadout
tap use
await app:loadout 8
wait 0.5
choose body
tap use
wait 0.5
tap use
wait 0.6
shot 13-the-wrap-on-and-packed with app:loadout
tap pause
tap pause
await app:none 4
await answered:cold 60
shot 14-and-the-wrap-answers-it with answered:cold,land:snowfield
